From: irisrun <irisrun@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:43:13 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 17/28] Add gradients, and draw them and drop shadows with the
 render core

Gradient was an empty stub and no gradient style existed. Gradient now has
stops, and LinearGradient, RadialGradient, AngularGradient and Color.gradient
are shape styles and views, with their ShapeStyle members. They resolve to a
paint the layer renderer hands to the render core: a gradient layer, masked
by the shape's path unless it is the layer's own rounded bounds. Text and
other places that take one color get the first stop's.

Shapes filled with paints other than one color crashed (render(paint:) was
unimplemented); they now fill the shape's path, with the style's opacity as
an effect. Drop shadows draw as the shadow of a render core group layer.
